15. Daily hassles (HS)-[POSITIVE]->Physical inactivity (SBQ)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'There is no known direct causal relationship where daily hassles (HS) cause physical inactivity (SBQ) or vice versa. Any potential association is likely mediated by variables such as perceived stress or depressive symptoms, which are present in the CLD. Therefore, a direct causal link should not be included. ', 'session_id': '5bef252f-f209-4274-9a39-33ae8001759a', 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3894304/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4128832/'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3894304/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited systematic review summarizes 168 studies and concludes that the majority show an inverse relationship between psychological stress and physical activity, with many prospective and diary studies (including daily-hassles measures) finding that higher stress/hassles predict reduced activity. It also cites some experimental/quasi-experimental evidence for acute stress reducing activity. However, the review documents notable heterogeneity (some studies show no effect or increased activity), identifies moderators (habitual exercisers, coping style, stage of change), and highlights methodological limits that preclude claiming a uniform direct causal effect of daily hassles on “becoming physically inactive” for all people. Thus the citations support a general tendency for hassles to reduce activity but not the strong, universal causal claim that people facing frequent daily hassles are “much more likely to avoid physical activity altogether.”"}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC4128832/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article studies an adapted daily-hassles scale in a low-income sample and examines associations with healthcare seeking (