   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Loneliness (UCLS) causes perceived social support (MSPSS) to change in an inverse relationship. Increased loneliness directly leads to decreased perceived social support, as individuals who feel lonelier tend to perceive less support from others. Conversely, decreased loneliness is causally linked to increased perceived social support.', 'session_id': '5bef252f-f209-4274-9a39-33ae8001759a', 'citations': ['https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12888-018-1736-5', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001691822001317', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5104760/', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001691825006286'], 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12888-018-1736-5", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited systematic review reports that loneliness and perceived social support are distinct but highly related subjective constructs and explicitly states that studies have found large negative correlations between loneliness and perceived social support. The review and the included studies consistently describe greater loneliness as associated with poorer (not greater) perceived social support; they do not provide evidence that loneliness increases sensitivity that would raise perceived social support. Therefore the citation contradicts, rather than supports, the proposed positive relationship."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001691822001317", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source contains only an error message and no usable content or evidence; therefore it provides no support for the claimed positive relationship or the explanatory mechanism.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0001691825006286", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited source provides only an error message and contains no substantive content or evidence about the relationship between loneliness and perceived social support, so it cannot support the claim.\\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED\\nSCORE: 0.0"}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5104760/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited study reports that higher loneliness is associated with lower perceived social support (e.g., single participants had higher romantic/family loneliness and lower MSPSS scores from significant others and family; MSPSS significant-other support was negatively related to romantic loneliness, β ≈ −0.24). The paper describes perceived support as a buffer that reduces loneliness and presents interactions where greater family or medium-high significant-other support mitigates loneliness. There is no evidence in the cited results that greater loneliness corresponds to higher perceived social support as claimed; the findings contradict that direction.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Experiencing loneliness can actually make people more aware of their social needs, prompting them to perceive even small acts of kindness as significant support. Therefore, higher loneliness might correlate with higher perceived social support, as individuals become more sensitive to positive social interactions.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Experiencing loneliness can actually make people more aware of their social needs, prompting them to perceive even small acts of kindness as significant support. Therefore, higher loneliness might correlate with higher perceived social support, as individuals become more sensitive to positive social interactions.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

