ecific relationship)."}], "aggregate_score": 0.1, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'There is no direct causal relationship where prosocial behavior (PGG) causes proinflammatory processes (TNF-alpha and IL-6) or vice versa. Any observed association is likely mediated by other variables such as stress, social support, or mental health in the system. Without a clear mechanistic pathway or evidence for direct causality, the relationship should not be included in the CLD.', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'perplexity': 1.3495011993449764, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8388208804985912, 'min_prob': 0.016005584278152178, 'token_prob_slope': -0.0027460563173822834, 'prob_variance': 0.06707294139186211, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9054400791692991, 'avg_nll': 0.2997350422083738}

