pedia.org/wiki/Prosocial_behavior", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited Wikipedia article on prosocial behavior does not state that there is no causal link between prosociality and spatial scale; instead it discusses prosociality across multiple social scales (schools, workplaces, communities), situational/group-size effects (e.g., bystander/diffusion of responsibility), and mechanisms (e.g., reciprocity, evolutionary arguments) that imply context- and scale-dependent relationships. It does not support the claim that no direct causal relationship exists between Prosocial behavior (PGG) and Spatial Scale; if anything, it indicates contextual/scale influences.  \\nVERDICT: NOT_SUPPORTED  \\nSCORE: 0.0"}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Prosocial behavior (PGG) does not cause Spatial Scale, nor does Spatial Scale cause Prosocial behavior (PGG). There is no direct causal relationship between these variables as defined. No mechanism exists by which a change in one would directly cause a change in the other.', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'perplexity': 1.2550823789504681, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8676963865828875, 'min_prob': 0.03644948687880808, 'token_prob_slope': -0.004567356186407912, 'prob_variance': 0.057154105265839736, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0996757775243482, 'avg_nll': 0.22720121102747998}

