that rumination reduces perceived social support or that others change their support in response to an individual\'s rumination. Therefore the specific claim is not supported by the provided citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.125, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) negatively impacts Perceived social support (MSPSS) because persistent self-focused thought patterns directly impair individuals’ cognitive capacity to recognize supportive behaviors from others. As rumination intensifies, individuals become less able to process external stimuli, which leads to an objective reduction in the actual support offered by their social network. Therefore, lower rumination enhances social environments, increasing the likelihood of receiving tangible support, as others respond primarily to the individual’s internal cognitive state.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.125, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Rumination (CERQ-R) negatively impacts Perceived social support (MSPSS) because persistent self-focused thought patterns directly impair individuals’ cognitive capacity to recognize supportive behaviors from others. As rumination intensifies, individuals become less able to process external stimuli, which leads to an objective reduction in the actual support offered by their social network. Therefore, lower rumination enhances social environments, increasing the likelihood of receiving tangible support, as others respond primarily to the individual’s internal cognitive state.', 'perplexity': 1.4305611320899652, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8266807554517623, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.0014725761344793703, 'token_prob_slope': -0.003332720747414579, 'prob_variance': 0.07341741203068226, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 0.9120225637694951, 'avg_nll': 0.3580667673659583}

