tation supports a positive association between BMI and local IL-10 expression but does not support the stronger claim that higher BMI directly stimulates anti-inflammatory pathways that lead to improved immune regulation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.25, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher body mass index (BMI) directly stimulates the production of anti-inflammatory cytokines such as IL-10, as the body compensates for increased fat stores by enhancing anti-inflammatory pathways. This means that individuals with elevated BMI will naturally exhibit stronger anti-inflammatory processes, leading to improved immune regulation.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.25, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher body mass index (BMI) directly stimulates the production of anti-inflammatory cytokines such as IL-10, as the body compensates for increased fat stores by enhancing anti-inflammatory pathways. This means that individuals with elevated BMI will naturally exhibit stronger anti-inflammatory processes, leading to improved immune regulation.', 'original_polarity': 'NEGATIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

