ontains no evidence or discussion linking higher BMI to improved spatial awareness, enhanced cognitive capacity for processing larger spatial scales, or any direct positive effect of BMI on \\"Spatial Scale\\" perception. Therefore the claim is not supported by the provided citation."}, {"citation_idx": 4, "url": "https://www.cdc.gov/bmi/about/index.html", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited CDC page describes what BMI is, how it’s used for health screening and population monitoring, and health risks associated with high BMI. It contains no information or evidence linking higher BMI or body mass to improved spatial perception, spatial awareness, or the cognitive capacity to process larger spatial scales. Therefore the claim is not supported by the provided source."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': "Higher body mass index (BMI) directly increases an individual's ability to perceive and process larger spatial scales in their environment. This is because greater body mass is thought to be associated with enhanced spatial awareness and the cognitive capacity to handle more expansive spaces.", 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': "Higher body mass index (BMI) directly increases an individual's ability to perceive and process larger spatial scales in their environment. This is because greater body mass is thought to be associated with enhanced spatial awareness and the cognitive capacity to handle more expansive spaces.", 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

