199. Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10)-[NEGATIVE]->Sleep disturbance (PSQI)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) cause sleep disturbance (PSQI) to change in an inverse relationship. Increased IL-10, an anti-inflammatory cytokine, directly reduces inflammatory activity, which is known to improve sleep quality and decrease sleep disturbances. Conversely, decreased IL-10 can lead to increased inflammation and worsen sleep disturbance. The causal direction is from anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to sleep disturbance (PSQI), not the reverse.', 'session_id': 'fb53e62f-ba3c-4c00-a381-8225eeec25a0', 'prob_std': 0.23830205780966512, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3410706/', 'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23490309/', 'https://www.nature.com/articles/npp2016148', 'https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/immunology/articles/10.3389/fimmu.2023.1161067/full', 'https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43440-021-00333-0'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7974773691267705, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3410706/", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review comprehensively covers IL-10 biology, regulation, and roles in infection, autoimmunity, and inflammation (including some CNS inflammatory models), but it does not present evidence linking IL-10 to sleep regulation or PSQI scores, nor does it describe the proposed neuronal mechanism (IL-10 increasing neuronal activity in sleep-regulating brain regions to reduce sleep need). There are no data or statements in the citation that support the causal directional claim between IL-10 levels and decreased sleep disturbance as measured by the PSQI."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/23490309/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited study reports a significant inverse association between circulating IL-10 and PSQI-measured poor sleep i