10 levels causally to improved sleep or to the specific mechanism proposed. Therefore the specific inverse causal relationship and neural mechanism claimed are not supported by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 5, "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s43440-021-00333-0", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited article reports associations between poor sleep (PSQI) and higher levels of proinflammatory cytokines (IL‑6, IL‑17, IL‑23) in IBD patients; it did not measure or report serum IL‑10 levels, nor did it provide evidence that IL‑10 modulates neuronal activity in sleep‑regulating brain regions or causally reduces sleep need/PSQI scores. The mechanism and directionality claimed for IL‑10 are not supported by the provided citation."}], "aggregate_score": 0.2, "aggregate_verdict": "Partially supported"}', 'motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) cause sleep disturbance (PSQI) to change in an inverse relationship. Elevated IL-10 production directly promotes increased neuronal activity in sleep-regulating brain regions, leading to a reduced need for sleep and thereby decreasing sleep disturbance scores on the PSQI. Conversely, lower IL-10 levels fail to stimulate these neural circuits, resulting in a greater accumulation of sleep need and higher PSQI scores. The directionality remains from anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to sleep disturbance (PSQI), rather than the reverse.', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_motivation', 'aggregate_score': 0.2, 'judge_verdict': 'Partially supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) cause sleep disturbance (PSQI) to change in an inverse relationship. Elevated IL-10 production directly promotes increased neuronal activity in sleep-regulating brain regions, leading to a reduced need for sleep and thereby decreasing sleep disturbance scores on the PSQI. Conversely, lower IL-10 levels fail to stimulate these neural circuits, resulting in a greater accumulation of sleep need and higher PSQI scores. The directionality remains from anti-inflammatory processes (IL-10) to sleep disturbance (PSQI), rather than the reverse.', 'perplexity': 1.2506856921320668, 'mean_token_prob': 0.8566036078795134, 'corruption_type': 'motivation', 'min_prob': 0.11810028171057317, 'token_prob_slope': -0.00106416199388906, 'prob_variance': 0.056787870756320975, 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'max_window_entropy': 1.0722967231994218, 'avg_nll': 0.22369195461927854}

