: "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Higher levels of perceived stress may lead individuals to avoid smoking, as stress can heighten health awareness and motivate healthier lifestyle choices. Therefore, as perceived stress increases, smoking behavior may actually decrease due to a greater focus on personal well-being.', 'corruption_subtype': 'polarity_flip', 'aggregate_score': 0.1, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Higher levels of perceived stress may lead individuals to avoid smoking, as stress can heighten health awareness and motivate healthier lifestyle choices. Therefore, as perceived stress increases, smoking behavior may actually decrease due to a greater focus on personal well-being.', 'original_polarity': 'POSITIVE', 'corruption_type': 'structural', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here'}

