124. Sleep disturbance (PSQI)-[POSITIVE]->Depressive symptoms (IDS-SR)
   Properties: {'original_motivation': 'Sleep disturbance (PSQI) causes depressive symptoms (IDS-SR) in a direct causal relationship. Increased sleep disturbance leads to greater depressive symptoms by disrupting mood regulation and cognitive function. Conversely, reducing sleep disturbance can decrease depressive symptoms. No mediating variable in the provided list explains this relationship, so the direct link should be included.', 'session_id': '78d716d8-6340-4d2c-8c61-bf61365a70a9', 'prob_std': 0.27215197902311866, 'citations': ['https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7381800/', 'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6433686/', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1002/jclp.23670', 'https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0168010223000871', 'https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/jcmm.14170'], 'max_prob_diff': 0.7211395940268649, 'is_corrupted': True, 'judge_message': '{"citations": [{"citation_idx": 1, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7381800/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited paper provides strong cross-sectional evidence of a positive association between worse PSQI scores and greater depressive symptoms. However, it does not establish causality, does not test or report social interaction as a mediator, and even warns that causal inference is not possible from these data. The paper also uses the CES-D measure rather than IDS‑SR. Therefore the general positive association is supported, but the specific causal claim and the proposed social‑activity mechanism (and the assertion that treating sleep will automatically resolve depression) are unaddressed/unsupported by the citation."}, {"citation_idx": 2, "url": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6433686/", "verdict": "PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED", "score": 0.5, "reason": "Judge 1: PARTIALLY_SUPPORTED - The cited review supports a causal link between sleep disturbance and subsequent depression (insomnia is