ly alters people’s exposure to such external stressors. The proposed behavioral pathway (IL-10 → suppressed physiological stress responses → fewer daily hassles encountered) is not shown in the cited material."}, {"citation_idx": 3, "url": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12974-016-0763-8", "verdict": "UNADDRESSED", "score": 0.0, "reason": "Judge 1: UNADDRESSED - The cited review documents IL-10’s anti‑inflammatory roles in the CNS, its cellular sources and regulation, and effects on neuroinflammation and neuroprotection. It does not provide evidence that higher IL-10 levels reduce the frequency of everyday “daily hassles” or directly suppress physiological stress responses in a way that lowers exposure to minor daily stressors. The specific behavioral/psychosocial link in the motivation is not examined in the paper."}], "aggregate_score": 0.0, "aggregate_verdict": "Not supported"}', 'motivation': 'Increased levels of the anti-inflammatory cytokine IL-10 directly reduce the frequency of daily hassles experienced by individuals by suppressing physiological stress responses. This makes people less likely to encounter minor daily stressors, as their bodies are better equipped to maintain homeostasis.', 'relevance': 'Auto-generated relevance here', 'corruption_subtype': 'spurious_edge', 'aggregate_score': 0.0, 'judge_verdict': 'Not supported', 'spurious_motivation': 'Increased levels of the anti-inflammatory cytokine IL-10 directly reduce the frequency of daily hassles experienced by individuals by suppressing physiological stress responses. This makes people less likely to encounter minor daily stressors, as their bodies are better equipped to maintain homeostasis.', 'corruption_type': 'structural'}

